{% assign pf = site.data.policy_feasibility %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/css/policy-feasibility.css' | relative_url | bust_file_cache }}">
<div
  id="policy-feasibility"
  class="pf-project pf-v2"
  data-pf-map="{{ '/assets/data/policy-feasibility/countries.geojson' | relative_url | bust_file_cache }}"
>
  <nav class="pf-stepnav" aria-label="Sections of this page">
    <ol>
      <li>
        <a href="#pf-top"><span class="pf-stepnav-number">·</span><span class="pf-stepnav-label">Framework</span></a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="#pf-define"><span class="pf-stepnav-number">01</span><span class="pf-stepnav-label">Question</span></a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="#pf-scope"><span class="pf-stepnav-number">02</span><span class="pf-stepnav-label">Outside view</span></a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="#pf-trajectories"><span class="pf-stepnav-number">03</span><span class="pf-stepnav-label">Trajectories</span></a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="#pf-assess"><span class="pf-stepnav-number">04</span><span class="pf-stepnav-label">Inside view</span></a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="#pf-model"><span class="pf-stepnav-number">05</span><span class="pf-stepnav-label">Scenario</span></a>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <header id="pf-top" class="pf-intro pf-reveal">
    <p class="pf-caption">
      A companion to the research article
      <a href="{{ pf.article_url }}"><em>The politics of baselines</em> · Fornborg (2026)</a>, published in ERSS
    </p>
    <p class="pf-intro-lead">
      Energy and climate scenarios rely on assumptions about future policy, but such policy trajectories are rarely screened for political feasibility
      before they enter models. The article develops a framework for doing so and demonstrates it ex post on a Swedish rail forecast from 1999. This
      page applies it ex ante, to a live question.
    </p>
    <p>
      The outside view scopes a limited set of candidate trajectories from precedent, institutional practice and actor positions. The inside view
      assesses each trajectory across five political dimensions. The scenario setting then decides how a trajectory enters the model: as the baseline,
      as a sensitivity case or as an alternative policy future.
    </p>
  </header>

  <figure class="pf-method pf-reveal" aria-labelledby="pf-framework-title">
    <figcaption>
      <h2 id="pf-framework-title">The framework</h2>
      <p>
        Following Kahneman and Lovallo (1993), the framework combines an outside view with an inside view. The outside view keeps scoping open enough
        to avoid tunnel vision; the inside view disciplines judgement once comparison begins.
      </p>
    </figcaption>
    <div class="pf-flow">
      <div class="pf-flow-group">
        <p class="pf-flow-label">Identify plausible trajectories</p>
        <a class="pf-flow-outside" href="#pf-scope"><strong>Outside view</strong><span>Places, time and actors</span></a>
        {% include policy-feasibility/flow-arrow.liquid step='outside' %}
        <a class="pf-flow-alternatives" href="#pf-trajectories"><strong>Candidate trajectories</strong><span>Expressed in modelling terms</span></a>
      </div>
      {% include policy-feasibility/flow-arrow.liquid step='inside' %}
      <a class="pf-flow-inside" href="#pf-assess"><strong>Inside view</strong><span>Five political dimensions</span></a>
      {% include policy-feasibility/flow-arrow.liquid step='scenario' %}
      <a class="pf-flow-scenario" href="#pf-model"><strong>Scenario use</strong><span>Baseline, sensitivity case or alternative future</span></a>
    </div>
  </figure>
  <nav class="pf-dimension-guide pf-reveal" aria-label="The five political dimensions">
    <p class="pf-caption">Five questions guide the assessment</p>
    <ol>
      {% for d in pf.dimensions %}
        <li>
          <a href="#pf-dimension-{{ d.id }}"
            ><strong>{{ d.name }}</strong><span>{{ d.guide }}</span></a
          >
        </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </nav>
  <p class="pf-intro-teaser pf-reveal">
    Quantification also shows why the specification of a trajectory matters: a requirement for new fossil-free generation can be met by contracting
    onshore wind that would be built anyway, so it changes the claim but not the electricity system. <a href="#pf-additionality">See 05</a>
  </p>

  <section id="pf-define" class="pf-section pf-case-intro pf-reveal">
    <div class="pf-case-copy">
      <p class="pf-step-tag">The case</p>
      <h2><span class="pf-section-number">01</span> The policy question</h2>
      <p class="pf-question">{{ pf.scope.question }}</p>
      <p class="pf-caption">Sweden · Policy decisions in {{ pf.decision_period }} · Rules from 2028 · Follow to {{ pf.model_horizon }}</p>
    </div>
    <img
      class="pf-case-illustration"
      src="{{ '/assets/images/policy-feasibility/datacenter-linework.png' | relative_url }}"
      alt=""
      width="1714"
      height="918"
      decoding="async"
    >
    <div class="pf-case-context">
      <figure>
        {% include policy-feasibility/tracker-map.liquid %}
        <figcaption>
          {{ site.data.policy_feasibility_context.metric }}.<br>
          Announced projects by {{ site.data.policy_feasibility_context.year }}.<br>
          <a href="{{ site.data.policy_feasibility_context.source_url | relative_url }}"
            >Tracker · {{ site.data.policy_feasibility_context.scenario_label -}}
          </a>
          · {{ site.data.policy_feasibility_context.snapshot_date | date: '%-d %B %Y' }}
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <h3>Why the rules are contested</h3>
        <ul class="pf-contested">
          <li>
            Announced datacenter projects would add about {{ site.data.policy_feasibility_scenarios.dc_load_twh.total | round }} TWh to Swedish
            electricity use by 2035, roughly a quarter of today’s use.
          </li>
          <li>
            Generation and grid capacity expand slowly: onshore wind depends on municipal approval, and offshore wind and new nuclear take years to
            permit and build.
          </li>
          <li>How the cost is shared between developers, households, industry and taxpayers is a political question.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% include policy-feasibility/next.liquid href='#pf-scope' number='02' title='Look across places and time' %}
  </section>

  {% include policy-feasibility/outside.liquid %}

  <section id="pf-trajectories" class="pf-section pf-reveal">
    <p class="pf-step-tag">From the outside view</p>
    <h2><span class="pf-section-number">03</span> Define comparable trajectories</h2>
    <p class="pf-prose">{{ pf.derivation }}</p>
    {% include policy-feasibility/trajectory-cards.liquid %}
    <p class="pf-specification-note">{{ pf.specification_note }}</p>
    <details class="pf-note">
      <summary>What the generation requirement covers</summary>
      <p>{{ pf.scope.definition }}</p>
      <p>{{ pf.scope.cohort }}</p>
      <p>{{ pf.scope.timing }}</p>
    </details>
    <details class="pf-note">
      <summary>Variants tested in the model</summary>
      <ul class="pf-variant-list">
        {% for v in pf.variants %}
          <li>
            <strong>{{ v.title }}</strong> <span class="pf-use pf-use-small">{{ v.scenario_use }}</span>
            <span>{{ v.text }}</span>
          </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </details>
    {% include policy-feasibility/next.liquid href='#pf-assess' number='04' title='Assess political feasibility' %}
  </section>

  {% include policy-feasibility/assess.liquid %}

  {% include policy-feasibility/scenario.liquid %}

  <div class="pf-sources-footer">
    <h2>Article and supporting material</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="{{ pf.article_url }}">The politics of baselines: A political feasibility framework for energy and climate scenarios</a>. David
      Fornborg, <em>Energy Research &amp; Social Science</em>, 141 (2026), 104981.
    </p>
    <div class="pf-links">
      <a href="{{ '/projects/political-feasibility/evidence/' | relative_url }}">Sources and evidence</a
      ><a href="{{ '/projects/datacenter-tracker/' | relative_url }}">Nordic datacenter tracker</a>
    </div>
    <p class="pf-caption">
      The tracker provides deployment context. This project assesses policy assumptions. The article develops the framework through a historical
      transport case.
    </p>
  </div>
  <script type="application/json" id="pf-case-data">
    {{ pf | jsonify | replace: '<', '<' }}
  </script>
</div>
<script defer src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/d3@7.9.0/dist/d3.min.js"></script>
<script defer src="{{ '/assets/js/policy-feasibility.js' | relative_url | bust_file_cache }}"></script>
